From: Brett Lamy <blamy@Bretts-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:53:56 -0500
Subject: Start recording for pages which are files

An Electron app's pages often are. They have no host, which is what a page
that isn't ready yet looks like otherwise.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/local_window_proxy.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/local_window_proxy.cc
index 6ffe488530677b828f8204a4c3c0232a7465e538..59e38d135db09ad1c2ddc43f5141f6c31ad67e2e 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/local_window_proxy.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/local_window_proxy.cc
@@ -240,8 +240,10 @@ void LocalWindowProxy::Initialize() {
     SetSecurityToken(origin.get());
   }
 
+  // An Electron app's pages are often files, which have no host. That's what a page
+  // which isn't ready yet looks like otherwise.
   if (recordreplay::IsRecordingOrReplaying("commands") &&
-      origin && !origin->Host().empty()) {
+      origin && (!origin->Host().empty() || origin->Protocol() == "file")) {
     bool initGlobally = !gRecordReplayStateInitialized;
 
     // Whether this is the relative root frame of this process.
